{"title":"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #16</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #15</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph shown at the right indicates the time taken by five people to travel various distances. On average, which person travelled the fastest?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c09ad7409cc88ed085852aee1793a1f96b4b996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\text{Allison} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\text{Bina} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\text{Curtis} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\text{Daniel} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{Emily}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"507\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d6580d98a69f52124868ab8537dfb8ff3a8c4f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = d/t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the average speed, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the distance, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is the time. We want to look for the highest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> among the people.\n</p><p>According to the graph, Allison traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometer in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes. This means that her speed was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb02bd84d9fe44f3a0f5f864a882a2d95c7084cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{20} = 0.05$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute.\n</p><p>Using the same method, we see that Bina traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometer in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes. This means that her speed was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6796e5522a58eeb9ab28559ed9c7be842b6c9182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{50} = 0.02$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute. This means that she was not the fastest, as her rate was lower than Allison's rate.\n</p><p>Curtis traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes. His rate was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d1d8829c2c5edab12f02eb06c6ce83f9171c405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{30} = \\frac{1}{10} = 0.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute, which was higher than Allison's rate. This means that he is the fastest so far.\n</p><p>Daniel traveled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes. His rate was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86cada29bf675492f07342fc82a62c5bc208dcf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{50} = \\frac{1}{10} = 0.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute. This was the same as the rate at which Curtis traveled, so neither of them were the fastest (according to the rules of the test, none of the problems had more than one answer).\n</p><p>Because all of the other answer choices have been eliminated, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf0b70d354140472f4ee05221faf23d06d627cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\text{Emily}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" />. We can also verify this by calculating Emily's rate, which was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d1a75600563ce4e87df46991528e1028faaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{20} = \\frac{1}{4} = 0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 1, we can use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d6580d98a69f52124868ab8537dfb8ff3a8c4f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = d/t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Without calculating the rates, we know that Bina could not have traveled the fastest because Bina took longer to travel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometer than Allison did. Similarly, we know that Daniel also couldn't have been the fastest because Daniel took longer than Emily to travel the same distance.\n</p><p>We also know that Allison was slower than Emily because she traveled a smaller distance in the same amount of time. \n</p><p>This means that we only need to compare the speed of Emily and Curtis. Using the same process as solution 1, we see that Daniel's rate was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86cada29bf675492f07342fc82a62c5bc208dcf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{50} = \\frac{1}{10} = 0.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute, and that Emily's rate was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d1a75600563ce4e87df46991528e1028faaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{20} = \\frac{1}{4} = 0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute.\n</p><p>Of these two, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf0b70d354140472f4ee05221faf23d06d627cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } \\text{Emily}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" /> was faster.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a h